  "notes": "Views identified as top, front, right-side, and isometric of the same clevis/yoke-style bracket. Title block states dimensions in millimetres and general tolerance +/-0.5; no feature dimensions are legible in the supplied image, so all geometry dimensions are estimated from proportions. Model uses X=front-view width, Y=vertical height, Z=depth. The two horizontal fork lugs are approximated as prism plates with octagonal/straight-segment rounded noses; true circular nose arcs are estimated. Rear upright block and sloped rear top seen in right-side/isometric views are represented by an added rear block plus a sloped side-web prism. Two coaxial vertical through holes in the top and bottom lugs are included as cut cylinders; the duplicate Hole entries record the physical holes in the requested XY hole list. Internal fork opening is represented by the gap between the two lug plates."
